		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4906&amp;p=35920#p35920"><![CDATA[
I wrote a long time ago about the problem of sound distortion, as well as the complete loss of decoding and receiving a signal from a neighboring timeslot. <br> At first, they told me that they couldn't repeat these mistakes. Then they said that the MD380UV/RT3S has a hardware error and the factory firmware has it too. I specially flashed the factory firmware and made observations - I did not hear any sound distortion, but there were cases of silence in the presence of a DMR signal. <br>I may be wrong, but at one time in older firmware versions, the error of modulating was extremely rare, when the error became more intense, I find it difficult to say. It is quite problematic to flash old firmware versions with old CPS, they are already lost. <br>Also, these errors are only present in duplex. Everything is fine in the simplex. This is probably why not everyone can detect them.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1432">EU1AEQ</a> — Tue Feb 25, 2025 12:14 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
